{
	id: "076A3B79E8E79DC5"
	group: "1A78C6EA3A0ABFDA"
	order_index: 7
	filename: "all_the_colors"
	title: "All the Colors"
	default_quest_shape: ""
	default_hide_dependency_lines: false
	quests: [
		{
			title: "Tales of Laughter"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "hexagon"
			description: [
				"&dOkay, we worked out that all the Tier 2 worlds in the FOP Game Server branch off of Tier 1 worlds. "
				""
				"&5To be fair to them, they DO have an image that shows this, but it was disabled last time we were able to check out the server."
				""
				"&dWhich was a long time ago... Well, you hold and Right Click a Blank Realmstone. Can't believe we forgot about that."
				""
				"&5Well, to be fair, I wouldn't be surprised if that was broken. The FOP have added, removed, and changed so many systems it's a wonder its only somewhat a buggy mess."
				""
				"&dWell, we have two destinations next, branching off of the first non-vanilla dimension: Lelyatia."
				""
				"&5And oooh boy are they doozies..."
				""
				"&dHonk Honk, brother."
			]
			dependencies: ["139A4328C69DF2C0"]
			id: "5CCB73FF0AB748D0"
			tasks: [{
				id: "34F44F360632CD06"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Realm of Facepaints"
			x: -5.25d
			y: -1.5d
			shape: "diamond"
			description: [
				"&5One of the two dimensions you can get to from Lelyatia is called Celeve. It's..."
				""
				"&d...a realm full of Clowns."
				""
				"&5It's a very strange and sad place. The worlds the FOP chooses for the Celeve spot don't start as clown worlds."
				""
				"&dThe world is controlled by the chief 'puppet master' of the FOP. We'll... talk about them later."
				""
				"&5Getting to the dimension is the concern. You'll need to visit Lelyatia, with a Blank Realmstone, a Crossbow, and some exploding Fireworks."
				""
				"&dYou'll need to make Fireworks WITH an Exploding Star, which is made by combining Gunpowder with any Dye."
				""
				"&5Then you need to kill a Lelytian Warrior with said Firework. That's where the Crossbow comes in. Put the stack of Fireworks in your offhand, and you'll load them into the Crossbow."
			]
			dependencies: ["5CCB73FF0AB748D0"]
			id: "18FC872BCD190C01"
			tasks: [{
				id: "558619AA2CD50D53"
				type: "item"
				item: "aoa3:celeve_realmstone"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "182B805B20B4433D"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Islands of Sad Joy"
			x: -3.5d
			y: -1.5d
			shape: "pentagon"
			description: [
				"&dRemember how Leyletia had two sides and how dangerous that could be? Well, this iteration of Celeve is much more dangerous."
				""
				"&5You'll want to bring some way to fly, grapple hook, or otherwise, Bandit. Celeve is a lot of floating islands over the void right now."
				""
				"&dThis is the punishment for fighting back too well against the FOP. Like we said before, the worlds that become Celeve don't start like this."
				""
				"&5Instead, the FOP punish worlds that succeed in some way in fighting back. A digital virus is introduced that turns everyone into Clowns, and their lands are torn asunder slowly."
			]
			dependencies: ["18FC872BCD190C01"]
			id: "15957CB357206700"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4B9AC4BAD13FD25E"
				type: "dimension"
				dimension: "aoa3:celeve"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "3C936D2EC21B40FB"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Circus Prizes"
			x: -1.5d
			y: -1.5d
			shape: "hexagon"
			description: [
				"&5Bandit, there really isn't any ore or gems or anything left in Celeve. The FOP made sure of that early on."
				""
				"&dThe only thing left for Celeve residents to survive on are various Clownish plants, and the gear and materials they can gather and salvage. They make the best of its, but the Clown virus has twisted them."
				""
				"&5Most hostile residents of Celeve have a chance of dropping Confetti Piles, the primary crafting component of most of their gear. They also may drop a special, final act of rebellion against the FOP: The Circus Coin, their own currency seperated from the FOP's scrypto."
				""
				"&dThe Circus Coin can be traded in to certain friendly Clowns. As for the Confetti, you can gather enough of it to make Hard Confetti Balls, useful for other crafts."
			]
			dependencies: ["15957CB357206700"]
			id: "2D2B122DDFFB7D30"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "0C226669EF9CBA4D"
					type: "item"
					item: "aoa3:confetti_pile"
				}
				{
